From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: denfry <dabinayo@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:55:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Spread player autosaves over the save interval

PlayerDataStorage writes to disk on the region thread, and with the
default settings a region saved up to 20 players in one tick. Players
that joined together are due together. On an idle disk this does not
show, but while the disk is busy each write can take 200-300 ms, and
with 30 bots and an autosave every 600 ticks the worst tick reached
3.4 s.

Without an explicit rate or max-per-tick, only as many players as the
interval needs are saved per tick. The worst tick in the same test
fell to 0.31 s. Explicit settings work as before.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java b/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java
index bbfa502da63063ba6cc62651cef7339bea867059..ba55ca2c8c758fa03034488ecbaa5ea96e66a43a 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java
@@ -1068,7 +1068,7 @@ public abstract class PlayerList {
                 profiler.startTimer(ca.spottedleaf.leafprofiler.LProfilerRegistry.PLAYER_SAVE); try { // Folia - profiler
                 this.save(player);
                 } finally { profiler.stopTimer(ca.spottedleaf.leafprofiler.LProfilerRegistry.PLAYER_SAVE); } // Folia - profiler
-                if (interval != -1 && ++numSaved >= io.papermc.paper.configuration.GlobalConfiguration.get().playerAutoSave.maxPerTick()) {
+                if (interval != -1 && ++numSaved >= io.papermc.paper.configuration.GlobalConfiguration.get().playerAutoSave.maxPerTick(interval, this.players.size())) { // Tessera - spread player autosaves over the save interval
                     break;
                 }
             }
